  "before_edn": "{:db/id 17592186166867 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186166720 :question/id #uuid \"58850b39-db80-532d-9f60-808a215da76c\" :question/math-academy-id \"e-9579\" :question/problem \"![](images/a9/a92eae1ab0af29ea895b570c95199ece1e292c09953ebb2dabbb7c6e2d422d6c.png)\\n\\nFind $\\\\dfrac{\\\\textrm{d}y}{\\\\textrm{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above.\" :question/worked-solution \"The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(3,-2).$\\n\\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\\n\\n$$\\ny^2 = 4px.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x = 3$ and $y = -2$ into the equation above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}(-2)^{2} & =4p(3) \\\\\\\\ 4 & =12p \\\\\\\\ p & =\\\\frac{1}{3}.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\ny^2 = \\\\dfrac{4}{3}x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\dfrac{\\\\textrm d y}{\\\\textrm d x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(\\\\frac{4}{3}x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\frac{4}{3} \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\frac{2}{3y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid \"53a1649d-4279-5b7c-839c-728f333b2c3f\" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186049118 :topic/difficulty 0.7541705546563298 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id 17592186428110 :encompassing/rationale \"Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 3 eligible passed source activities = 0.333333; nearest selected fraction = 1/3. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1/3 (1/3). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 1124->2978. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json.\" :encompassing/topic {:db/id 17592186049178} :encompassing/weight 0.3333333333333333}] :topic/id #uuid \"dc0c57dc-d0cc-5d0f-bc3f-5c52faa2e959\" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id 17592186096702} {:db/id 17592186096703} {:db/id 17592186096704} {:db/id 17592186096705}] :topic/math-academy-id 1124 :topic/next [{:db/id 17592186048350} {:db/id 17592186048559} {:db/id 17592186048894} {:db/id 17592186049336} {:db/id 17592186049506} {:db/id 17592186050769} {:db/id 17592186051063}] :topic/title \"Left and Right Opening Parabolas\"}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id 17592186550211 :question-generator/id #uuid \"e359bb2a-e736-568f-8841-85888e3467e5\" :question-generator/script \"generate/scratch/17592186166867.py\"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186167095 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"d0573536-31f0-563b-9d07-911863e634bc\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{y}{2}\" :db/id 17592186163649} {:answer/id #uuid \"d09192f8-b86c-51d6-a122-7afcd699607f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{2}{y}\" :db/id 17592186163650} {:answer/id #uuid \"d9efdc1d-d656-5d1e-83d6-ccd7d0ea85d2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2}{y}\" :db/id 17592186163651} {:answer/id #uuid \"f4600882-36d2-52ce-8da2-b54d8b2af6df\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{4}{y}\" :db/id 17592186163652} {:answer/id #uuid \"2e3b5a55-f245-5539-8b5a-59cf6f8686da\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4y\" :db/id 17592186163653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"d9efdc1d-d656-5d1e-83d6-ccd7d0ea85d2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2}{y}\" :db/id 17592186163651} :answer-field/id #uuid \"41202eeb-84d9-576f-9f59-f15c773b23c1\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186163648}] :question/id #uuid \"0981d1d8-5908-5954-92c8-10f4e8de0d4e\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-127372\" :question/problem \"![](images/00/0030e466a772b1ccd61140453c5e0e50ff365a0bf42034422bce9e1691983c43.png)\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{dy}{dx}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above.\" :question/worked-solution \"The right-opening parabola has vertex $(0,0)$ and passes through $(1,2)$. Its equation is $y^2=4x$. Differentiate to obtain $2yy'=4$, so $$\\\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\\\frac2y$$ for $y\\\\ne0$.\"} {:db/id 17592186167096 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"b50d0c40-6788-57f6-abfc-e79bf313d479\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{y}{2}\" :db/id 17592186163655} {:answer/id #uuid \"0872fa03-25f1-5ab1-8e8a-b7add5e28113\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{y}\" :db/id 17592186163656} {:answer/id #uuid \"40308631-4569-53b4-a049-a0c1e9473978\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{1}{y}\" :db/id 17592186163657} {:answer/id #uuid \"515e1940-de9b-5005-bcc4-522fce4979f6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{2}{y}\" :db/id 17592186163658} {:answer/id #uuid \"77251aea-0d1b-53cd-8e9c-1840b159150c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{1}{2y}\" :db/id 17592186163659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"40308631-4569-53b4-a049-a0c1e9473978\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{1}{y}\" :db/id 17592186163657} :answer-field/id #uuid \"106254b3-fb7a-53e5-9145-bedbc3b56b87\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186163654}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"2b2fc0d7-ecff-5b63-8ad8-a6faaff8e7b2\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-127374\" :question/problem \"![](images/88/88bec66b7ece961f2f0fc4083ce317f2bdc414e0a219d61bbf9bf73ae667ca0f.png)\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above.\" :question/worked-solution \"The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-2,2).$\\n\\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=4px.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=-2$ and $y=2$ into the equation above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}(2)^{2} & =4p(-2) \\\\\\\\ 4 & =-8p \\\\\\\\ p & =-\\\\frac{1}{2}.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=-2x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(-2x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =-2 \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =-\\\\frac{1}{y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186262782 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"219845eb-d05c-53b6-8c35-514bf8a6a3e8\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{1}{2y}\" :db/id 17592186260163} {:answer/id #uuid \"2cbaa061-8eee-52ef-b708-518d83dacbe3\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{6}{y}\" :db/id 17592186260277} {:answer/id #uuid \"6a53e920-1f56-54ef-9a0d-a07c822f8f3d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{1}{6y}\" :db/id 17592186260807} {:answer/id #uuid \"6f270028-5c9b-5ad1-bf83-211b5d81af31\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2}{y}\" :db/id 17592186260852} {:answer/id #uuid \"d675cc22-4e88-5836-a463-6a2f29d37cb6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{2y}\" :db/id 17592186261761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"2cbaa061-8eee-52ef-b708-518d83dacbe3\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{6}{y}\" :db/id 17592186260277} :answer-field/id #uuid \"4ac39f57-fa34-5bb6-bec8-a47660173164\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186262255}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"d5970e3a-67be-579a-8f6a-680fce2bb7ff\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-127510\" :question/problem \"![](images/e0/e0d18f7db92cfbe372f998e69d2395f2d586eb36cd25773588149c4ccf678eba.png)\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above.\" :question/worked-solution \"The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(3,6).$\\n\\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(3,6)$ is given by\\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=4px.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=3$ and $y=6$ into the equation above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}(6)^{2} & =4p(3) \\\\\\\\ 36 & =12p \\\\\\\\ p & =3.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=12x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(12x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =12 \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\frac{6}{y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186262787 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"53b126be-2e72-5683-87f0-2bce708ce0b3\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{2}{y}\" :db/id 17592186260580} {:answer/id #uuid \"ac29313d-f700-5356-b3ea-db25827d7000\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{1}{y}\" :db/id 17592186261378} {:answer/id #uuid \"af2deb81-9196-5179-b2ff-4e88fe6ffef3\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2y}\" :db/id 17592186261420} {:answer/id #uuid \"c2ee63f7-23d8-539c-8477-779c46a531e2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2}{y}\" :db/id 17592186261595} {:answer/id #uuid \"d1164fca-4cb8-5220-a316-6ca8fe78ed20\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{y}\" :db/id 17592186261719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"53b126be-2e72-5683-87f0-2bce708ce0b3\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{2}{y}\" :db/id 17592186260580} :answer-field/id #uuid \"4c21556d-ce63-50ba-aa4c-f313d47a9e13\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186262257}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"b2ff195e-41e9-5105-9c9e-ed134d28a53d\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-127515\" :question/problem \"![](images/5e/5eedb15e515993bdc8a2ee37ab4c7c0e0225b9d2118d5d60e8593de5ea56f199.png)\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above.\" :question/worked-solution \"The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-1,2).$\\n\\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=4px.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=-1$ and $y=2$ into the equation above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}(2)^{2} & =4p(-1) \\\\\\\\ 4 & =-4p \\\\\\\\ p & =-1.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=-4x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(-4x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =-4 \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =-\\\\frac{2}{y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186262788 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"05cc5c38-3fac-504b-a52a-dbbcc512e957\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{2}{y}\" :db/id 17592186259926} {:answer/id #uuid \"46b94c76-6f4b-5df7-afa2-245210c1a600\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{1}{y}\" :db/id 17592186260489} {:answer/id #uuid \"5ac2c1f5-97e4-55ee-8c09-94a6ec7fc43d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{4y}\" :db/id 17592186260651} {:answer/id #uuid \"7dc8ab5c-9f98-553d-8e5c-4e7a8e4f49d9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{1}{2y}\" :db/id 17592186260970} {:answer/id #uuid \"aa32c440-9d05-5e9e-95fc-705f2a3492a7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{y}\" :db/id 17592186261364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"46b94c76-6f4b-5df7-afa2-245210c1a600\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{1}{y}\" :db/id 17592186260489} :answer-field/id #uuid \"fb45d64f-7844-5746-b5c9-fba237c20fd2\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186262562}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"72fb768f-c740-5cf4-b10e-4551f1d715de\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-127520\" :question/problem \"![](images/60/60987d053d138d4a26cbc05adccb0da23810f97243f9399d3fe401a0202394b0.png)\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above.\" :question/worked-solution \"The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-8,4).$\\n\\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=4px.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=-8$ and $y=4$ into the equation above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}(4)^{2} & =4p(-8) \\\\\\\\ 16 & =-32p \\\\\\\\ p & =-\\\\frac{1}{2}.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=-2x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(-2x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =-2 \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =-\\\\frac{1}{y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186297360 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"18f6ba14-67bb-52a5-83f3-90748a808eb7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{49}{10y}\" :db/id 17592186295413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"18f6ba14-67bb-52a5-83f3-90748a808eb7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{49}{10y}\" :db/id 17592186295413} :answer-field/id #uuid \"6ea47b69-ba23-5df0-89cb-9a0a8a5b3195\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186296865}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"2b5b23fa-be02-551f-968d-c9191c07be80\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-312780\" :question/problem \"![](images/b2/b269001ff5a3a1a1d86125157ee2f5b77d89ebcf0041f8d403dbc931b796c5e8.png)\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\\n\\n$\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}=$\\n{{field-1}}\" :question/worked-solution \"The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(5,7).$\\n\\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=4px.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=5$ and $y=7$ into the equation above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}(7)^{2} & =4p(5) \\\\\\\\ 49 & =20p \\\\\\\\ p & =\\\\frac{49}{20}.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=\\\\frac{49}{5}x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(\\\\frac{49}{5}x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\frac{49}{5} \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\frac{49}{10y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186317217 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"08ce1afa-8b88-5a8a-8cdc-4e464a1bb102\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{1}{6y}\" :db/id 17592186315162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"08ce1afa-8b88-5a8a-8cdc-4e464a1bb102\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{1}{6y}\" :db/id 17592186315162} :answer-field/id #uuid \"4ad31bfe-fcf5-5162-a8e6-4281f1f124b2\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186316722}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"28f921c8-6fd7-5d79-b2ff-0d1df567197f\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-342215\" :question/problem \"![](images/c4/c403f11093b76facafbecb72bcc413640ac67fe6ed73d6b64374230f39e29aba.png)\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\\n\\n$\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}=$\\n{{field-1}}\" :question/worked-solution \"The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-3,-1).$\\n\\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=4px.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=-3$ and $y=-1$ into the equation above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{2} & =4p(-3) \\\\\\\\ 1 & =-12p \\\\\\\\ p & =-\\\\frac{1}{12}.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=-\\\\frac{1}{3}x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(-\\\\frac{1}{3}x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =-\\\\frac{1}{3} \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =-\\\\frac{1}{6y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186317218 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"ad5bf0a8-9d5e-50fe-96f9-d4d663d3f517\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{3}{y}\" :db/id 17592186316094}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"ad5bf0a8-9d5e-50fe-96f9-d4d663d3f517\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{3}{y}\" :db/id 17592186316094} :answer-field/id #uuid \"12408f4c-1370-5d9b-b3b2-f660b8736202\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186316591}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"a43aa514-b6a3-516e-bf25-cd1e713491f7\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-342218\" :question/problem \"![](images/73/7367cb4ae1feb4e18b98b712687ceb4a1db67f8c9e4965af3ffd1253a827f346.png)\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\\n\\n$\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}=$\\n{{field-1}}\" :question/worked-solution \"The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-6,6).$\\n\\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=4px.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=-6$ and $y=6$ into the equation above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}{6}^{2} & =4p(-6) \\\\\\\\ 36 & =-24p \\\\\\\\ p & =-\\\\frac{3}{2}.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=-6x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(-6x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =-6 \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =-\\\\frac{3}{y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186317243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"4203b15d-0bea-5e2b-934d-26d20084a739\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{y}\" :db/id 17592186315503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"4203b15d-0bea-5e2b-934d-26d20084a739\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{y}\" :db/id 17592186315503} :answer-field/id #uuid \"fd3bd66b-afeb-5b87-8ae5-7c88b3e0adad\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186317149}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"3b67c83b-c5b3-5c60-b778-f810479299ef\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-342354\" :question/problem \"![](images/85/85d75e0f3a9f2a30282d1f1754b0c46da49e8f73ff2a858c856ba5492eb21cca.png)\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\\n\\n$\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}=$\\n{{field-1}}\" :question/worked-solution \"The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(8,-8).$\\n\\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=4px.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=8$ and $y=-8$ into the equation above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}(-8)^{2} & =4p(8) \\\\\\\\ 64 & =32p \\\\\\\\ p & =2.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=8x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(8x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =8 \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\frac{4}{y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186317244 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"b26c1af7-9a5b-5d43-b1b5-dc74de3adf12\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{3y}\" :db/id 17592186316127}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"b26c1af7-9a5b-5d43-b1b5-dc74de3adf12\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{3y}\" :db/id 17592186316127} :answer-field/id #uuid \"52a041cb-28c3-51b4-b579-c9bbf60ee415\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186316739}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"c82bb467-368a-5a4c-94f6-b887899fd25e\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-342355\" :question/problem \"![](images/1a/1aab10c5376ca6ae6c43829bc6f7617fb236b24c883d8ad61c47b83b75511d5a.png)\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\\n\\n$\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}=$\\n{{field-1}}\" :question/worked-solution \"The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(6,-2).$\\n\\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=4px.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=6$ and $y=-2$ into the equation above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}(-2)^{2} & =4p(6) \\\\\\\\ 4 & =24p \\\\\\\\ p & =\\\\frac{1}{6}.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=\\\\frac{2}{3}x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(\\\\frac{2}{3}x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\frac{2}{3} \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\frac{1}{3y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186508059 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"5efdb2c0-9881-5a00-b565-3f359e70c7a7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{9y}{2}\" :db/id 17592186507737} {:answer/id #uuid \"93f161f4-832c-5426-af71-c7778005d5fb\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{3}{4y}\" :db/id 17592186507807} {:answer/id #uuid \"e3a24980-5105-538e-8c74-64c4ebc803d1\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3y}{4}\" :db/id 17592186507904} {:answer/id #uuid \"e5c9d2d6-91af-5536-9214-6c10a18ce267\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{9}{2y}\" :db/id 17592186507909} {:answer/id #uuid \"ef20abea-8c5e-5aa2-aa09-5d4772fb2a0c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{9}{4y}\" :db/id 17592186507922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"ef20abea-8c5e-5aa2-aa09-5d4772fb2a0c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{9}{4y}\" :db/id 17592186507922} :answer-field/id #uuid \"293366ad-ad39-5d08-a9c8-a7c1154b5526\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186507956}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"3f2a3f8a-3c25-5094-b1ff-9932bec29ec7\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-127503\" :question/problem \"![](images/4c/4c6a99f62a77f7fc16dbb95e8a8d03c42b266fffee10ed3739ab13820729be44.png)\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above.\" :question/worked-solution \"The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(2,-3).$\\n\\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=4px.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=2$ and $y=-3$ into the equation above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}(-3)^{2} & =4p(2) \\\\\\\\ 9 & =8p \\\\\\\\ p & =\\\\frac{9}{8}.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=\\\\frac{9}{2}x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(\\\\frac{9}{2}x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\frac{9}{2} \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\frac{9}{4y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186550175 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"7904e266-8e40-55dd-9fdd-7cf84c6b8ee2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{6}{y}\" :db/id 17592186550183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"7904e266-8e40-55dd-9fdd-7cf84c6b8ee2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{6}{y}\" :db/id 17592186550183} :answer-field/id #uuid \"eb810b16-9131-57df-8426-531a34ce6789\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186550207}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"50ce0446-d663-52f1-8947-55316401966e\" :question/problem \"![](images/44/44f13c74646a1a3dda14673314c545a5909a72b05ba9f967ebcaff36f7388b76.png)\\n\\nThe parabola shown above has equation\\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=12x.\\n$$\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\\n\\n$\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}=$\\n{{field-1}}\" :question/worked-solution \"The equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=12x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(12x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =12 \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\frac{6}{y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186550181 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"00e669d2-14d3-5434-9211-5869010d936c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"1\" :db/id 17592186550170} {:answer/id #uuid \"2e2c26d1-ec58-5ccd-9713-dc626a6a709b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2}{y}\" :db/id 17592186550174} {:answer/id #uuid \"631196e3-5519-58d7-8473-4cb19b848b22\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{y}\" :db/id 17592186550179} {:answer/id #uuid \"bfd36e2a-37e1-5b00-b514-1c3a7e896da5\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{1}{y}\" :db/id 17592186550195} {:answer/id #uuid \"d0179ef3-c580-5528-84e0-df55b78be308\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"y\" :db/id 17592186550199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"631196e3-5519-58d7-8473-4cb19b848b22\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{y}\" :db/id 17592186550179} :answer-field/id #uuid \"949c86c3-1387-5e76-838f-1ec7b8fcfcfa\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186550188}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"6d66d3ac-d9e8-5dde-9473-af7404844f56\" :question/problem \"![](images/a1/a1617023328f096064631df2281e8a3c2eeb471ee4676f937226eb0d1da378d8.png)\\n\\nThe parabola shown above has equation\\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=2x.\\n$$\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above.\" :question/worked-solution \"The equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=2x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(2x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =2 \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\frac{1}{y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186550186 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"7bb2b4ad-8fa6-5ac0-8fd7-24f6ea1af156\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{25}{2y}\" :db/id 17592186550185} {:answer/id #uuid \"b276fc34-6866-5aa2-b322-57858b47dcfd\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2y}{25}\" :db/id 17592186550192} {:answer/id #uuid \"db628145-c476-5119-b18e-7eb7e30a50c0\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{25}{y}\" :db/id 17592186550202} {:answer/id #uuid \"e6a6b16d-c4b5-5137-b1e8-df151019da65\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{25}{2}\" :db/id 17592186550205} {:answer/id #uuid \"e7fa4761-ecc5-554e-8011-3b2b816babd3\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{25}{2y}\" :db/id 17592186550206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"e7fa4761-ecc5-554e-8011-3b2b816babd3\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{25}{2y}\" :db/id 17592186550206} :answer-field/id #uuid \"c36fc50e-5f0b-5a61-8bdb-da8f79c138e9\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186550196}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"7bb4752b-36a2-5de3-a203-84e3b9f073de\" :question/problem \"![](images/61/61d540bfd94984bf7a96a5981ca65233399beec607d469fc1641b2326826a4d4.png)\\n\\nThe parabola shown above has equation\\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=25x.\\n$$\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above.\" :question/worked-solution \"The equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=25x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(25x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =25 \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\frac{25}{2y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186550187 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"1dcae4f4-f85b-5c2d-9a5c-77a94b0d19ba\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{4y}{3}\" :db/id 17592186550171} {:answer/id #uuid \"28b78bcf-a12c-569a-bb17-9e66db7be89e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{4y}\" :db/id 17592186550173} {:answer/id #uuid \"6dcfe650-ba97-586c-9fa2-c5fd10d5d462\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{3}{4}\" :db/id 17592186550182} {:answer/id #uuid \"a77383dc-b83a-560c-83e8-3d350ee2aea0\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{3}{4y}\" :db/id 17592186550190} {:answer/id #uuid \"af1c4627-36c6-5ae9-993e-1728a7e2772f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{3}{2y}\" :db/id 17592186550191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"a77383dc-b83a-560c-83e8-3d350ee2aea0\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{3}{4y}\" :db/id 17592186550190} :answer-field/id #uuid \"b4a49c6e-ae2b-5f68-b70a-03e4f0368e1c\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186550193}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"8f4d582e-5489-5989-8e7a-5c782843e1d4\" :question/problem \"![](images/a7/a7c56fd2bfe1aa346bcebdf79f128140235c69fd72cf5b147eace57827fe9689.png)\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above.\" :question/worked-solution \"The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-6,-3).$\\n\\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=4px.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=-6$ and $y=-3$ into the equation above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}(-3)^{2} & =4p(-6) \\\\\\\\ 9 & =-24p \\\\\\\\ p & =-\\\\frac{3}{8}.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=-\\\\frac{3}{2}x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(-\\\\frac{3}{2}x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =-\\\\frac{3}{2} \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =-\\\\frac{3}{4y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186550198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"57e246f3-cb19-54af-a1b3-e2c195a5e06e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{2y}\" :db/id 17592186550177} {:answer/id #uuid \"5e758806-41e5-566a-bd49-b8b45956c8f5\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{3}{4y}\" :db/id 17592186550178} {:answer/id #uuid \"7a61b366-e9b7-591e-8aa3-cb81c88d5dc9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{4y}\" :db/id 17592186550184} {:answer/id #uuid \"e2d2e80c-ed1d-537f-9327-a685067c2765\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{4}\" :db/id 17592186550204} {:answer/id #uuid \"f437c276-f770-525e-91cd-572b961b92ac\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4y}{3}\" :db/id 17592186550210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"7a61b366-e9b7-591e-8aa3-cb81c88d5dc9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{4y}\" :db/id 17592186550184} :answer-field/id #uuid \"c7e14ab2-deee-519b-b7a6-3593e9d0bdd8\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186550197}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"cd0c7321-e023-5633-bdad-071f1a7eccfc\" :question/problem \"![](images/00/0012f2c4830f5acc401b551e8421b0bbb730c2e27f68010a691d74dcfd6ea93a.png)\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above.\" :question/worked-solution \"The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(6,-3).$\\n\\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=4px.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=6$ and $y=-3$ into the equation above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}(-3)^{2} & =4p(6) \\\\\\\\ 9 & =24p \\\\\\\\ p & =\\\\frac{3}{8}.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=\\\\frac{3}{2}x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(\\\\frac{3}{2}x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\frac{3}{2} \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\frac{3}{4y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186550201 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"53593d78-cb2e-5976-b61a-00fc854f664f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{4}{y}\" :db/id 17592186550176} {:answer/id #uuid \"68a12903-3439-50f4-80b6-1bf16f06ff09\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{y}\" :db/id 17592186550180} {:answer/id #uuid \"bb62951c-7be2-5985-89a7-796fe92d0fe7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\" :db/id 17592186550194} {:answer/id #uuid \"d2f3ef9c-8be7-525c-bc57-d1ce7659ff00\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{8}{y}\" :db/id 17592186550200} {:answer/id #uuid \"f14e21d6-640a-5340-bceb-b2ba5f8abe44\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{y}{4}\" :db/id 17592186550208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"68a12903-3439-50f4-80b6-1bf16f06ff09\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{y}\" :db/id 17592186550180} :answer-field/id #uuid \"f232da10-2779-54d0-8c60-da3948a8ec17\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186550209}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"d4eb74b6-db84-5116-8322-9b24d0326181\" :question/problem \"![](images/03/03a879d7f79141f6816bf74a73efa87b089e2c213bc2b58bc93727cd8ee08500.png)\\n\\nThe parabola shown above has equation\\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=8x.\\n$$\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above.\" :question/worked-solution \"The equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=8x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(8x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =8 \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\frac{4}{y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186550203 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"2894d3a0-b026-5675-b147-35e34dd8a2d1\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2y}\" :db/id 17592186550172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"2894d3a0-b026-5675-b147-35e34dd8a2d1\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2y}\" :db/id 17592186550172} :answer-field/id #uuid \"94b609e7-041d-52dc-a078-56c86fba7886\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186550189}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"dcf749a6-fb83-5c81-b302-2511741ae8e2\" :question/problem \"![](images/19/19065a69504e6bd90d36a7804f05ce9952a90c838c1ddb43c374e53ccbf038a7.png)\\n\\nThe parabola shown above has equation\\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=1x.\\n$$\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\\n\\n$\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}=$\\n{{field-1}}\" :question/worked-solution \"The equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=1x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(1x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\frac{1}{2y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186656935 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"010e431e-2442-595f-b58f-7395c7a2ac4d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{y}{2}\" :db/id 17592186656387} {:answer/id #uuid \"49bbf2de-9d18-5871-b538-74cfe0a7c8ea\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2y}\" :db/id 17592186656488} {:answer/id #uuid \"8971c208-368c-5b93-8184-03df20eae652\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{y}\" :db/id 17592186656592} {:answer/id #uuid \"c14c54d0-314d-5621-bdd4-18d15e6b3bee\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{y}{4}\" :db/id 17592186656670} {:answer/id #uuid \"ebf236bc-0c37-5680-868d-81f9aab6d958\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-\\\\frac{2}{y}\" :db/id 17592186656730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"8971c208-368c-5b93-8184-03df20eae652\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{y}\" :db/id 17592186656592} :answer-field/id #uuid \"b1ed141e-2053-5309-a1a8-f4c6aea7a6e3\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186656827}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"ba669e01-0424-5360-b582-c8ddd3a27bb6\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-127507\" :question/problem \"![](images/0f/0fb6e28df6459782453b94a7516d47407e3625fc13609ab2b85e7e5e2ac597f4.png)\\n\\nFind $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above.\" :question/worked-solution \"The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(2,4).$\\n\\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=4px.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=2$ and $y=4$ into the equation above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}(4)^{2} & =4p(2) \\\\\\\\ 16 & =8p \\\\\\\\ p & =2.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \\n\\n$$\\n{y}^{2}=8x.\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, to calculate $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}}{\\\\text{d}x}(8x) \\\\\\\\ 2y\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =8 \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\frac{4}{y}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"}] :knowledge-point/title \"Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parabola\"}",
  "records": []
}
